{"id": "clm:8138960186eb95769a5989c468c501b4b29918b28cd42ad02299addfb48c40e3", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas snapshot distribution is an opt-in Cloud Backup policy that copies selected cluster snapshots from the primary region to additional regions within the same cloud provider. Policy items set a destination region, snapshot frequency or a number of recent snapshots, and copy retention. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "definition", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/blob/master/docs/resources/cloud_backup_schedule.md", "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-set-up-cross-region-backup-atlas/view"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1bd0d0cdba021e287f0a7f74468ef5898f6cd127ebc8564cdf964d0765d9a4e9", "ev:8eb1a409a820cd1722ac12334b9c0456b333c2c527a7b78520055985adec1d4d", "ev:f57d46845581198c555f7e3d422dfab128e9779f6a66d3675e2508cda84831dd"]}
{"id": "clm:3f058c3bf6da1135573c5838cc25759f269b83a0aa5a2524e8c79c5b9123f9cd", "type": "statement", "text": "Copying snapshots to other regions adds cross-region data-transfer charges and snapshot-storage charges in those regions. PointFive recommends reducing copy regions or copied snapshot types when disaster-recovery requirements do not justify the additional copies. (medium confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/billing/cluster-configuration-costs.md", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.pointfive.co/efficiency-hub/inefficiencies/excessive-snapshot-retention-and-cross-region-copies-in-mongodb-atlas-cloud-backup"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:c854ea1b580ea48c384f9c49ac0bb3f17915a6f112cad749ac7a758984d7d9a8", "ev:d676fe9d6059636754c6bf6f502f0d6d73283a2bd6adb943253f698d2d868fde"]}
{"id": "clm:a517123522b10b86ebb4c433c4ce263596d4fa2231470957a37fd15402fa7c25", "type": "statement", "text": "For a multi-region restore, local copies in the target cluster's regions can allow Atlas to use faster direct-attach restores when the target is in the same project and regions as those copies. If a local copy is unavailable or the target uses NVMe storage, Atlas defaults to slower streaming restore; snapshot distribution therefore does not guarantee a fixed restore time. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "mechanism", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/backups/", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/disaster-recovery.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:183350e795d0bcdb5a59fbea12547acaf8b0f710482213027aa342433f83a918", "ev:a7cf9347332532c2d5f2ab89bcab31db6188a7fceb87db0fcfc98c82e72b884f"]}
{"id": "clm:713413604e41cf4af3125cbacb555f65ae27caadb3b5e3c3d6e2ef1203b28458", "type": "statement", "text": "When copies exist in every region of a multi-region cluster, Atlas can use faster direct-attach restores from local copies after a regional outage instead of slower cross-region streaming restores. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "comparisons", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/disaster-recovery.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:64967aaa08bf25fe20d5068a45f951c3debff1b538fda4d248a70da10bfe680f", "ev:a7cf9347332532c2d5f2ab89bcab31db6188a7fceb87db0fcfc98c82e72b884f"]}
{"id": "clm:3d190f736b688e6edea7c454186c30fd1e4978031a0bb949534817c2d669d936", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas Cloud Backup stores snapshots in the cloud provider region of the cluster's current primary node by default. A snapshot copy policy distributes copies to additional regions; its policy items specify the target region, copy frequency, retention time, and whether to copy oplogs. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/blob/master/docs/resources/cloud_backup_schedule.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:1bd0d0cdba021e287f0a7f74468ef5898f6cd127ebc8564cdf964d0765d9a4e9"]}
{"id": "clm:6d55946a71eac72e36b4e791eac475145e84a7b39f59161a2c141b6ade8dda8c", "type": "statement", "text": "Point-in-time restore from a copy region requires Continuous Cloud Backup and oplog copying to that region. Oplog copying is enabled at the region level, so enabling it for one policy item makes point-in-time restore available for all snapshot-copy policies in that region. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/blob/master/docs/resources/cloud_backup_schedule.md"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8a4a152a8f73ee25a2f551c5f682b07670acf1fa2504315f7fb997649d664d13", "ev:8d7a0a19898cfa6b632b513a93e6212366e5c280d050b949b5974b6a0257ac35"]}
{"id": "clm:9708e348cd7c656a3b491311ea976e96362e7d1f6e118981afa9472f540d46f2", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas requires snapshot copy regions to use the same cloud provider as the cluster's primary region. (high confidence)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-set-up-cross-region-backup-atlas/view"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:8eb1a409a820cd1722ac12334b9c0456b333c2c527a7b78520055985adec1d4d"]}
{"id": "clm:86984a2dd41357d518f15f48e06c59788c8df99d6dac0690d18a1151ddeab544", "type": "statement", "text": "The current Atlas snapshot-distribution documentation says the feature is not supported on Atlas Infinite clusters during public preview. (high confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/infinite/atlas-infinite-landing/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:524c0ca8d6bcaf1384eefc34c5ad5436ff6ba96a5a1bb0ad9ab8760b27c28bb6", "ev:5908f1fa558a34364562c23814bc9e20d06a0b4418b8fbf0a0917e76c5db3aa1"]}
{"id": "clm:b1d7fd37fc616390f20f58652edea6fdb1bf874279c962951195c7f89fd8e344", "type": "statement", "text": "MongoDB's February 17, 2026 announcement describes controls for selecting snapshots, setting copy retention independently from source snapshots, and applying policy changes to existing copies. The Terraform provider documents copy_policy_items or last_number_of_snapshots selection and update_copy_snapshots or delete_copy_snapshots controls. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/product-release-announcements/introducing-enhanced-control-for-cross-region-snapshots", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://github.com/mongodb/terraform-provider-mongodbatlas/blob/master/docs/resources/cloud_backup_schedule.md", "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:980080130dad66cbc89d330bff2014f00c4457fba58c85fcad8c33f57e0ac7ab", "ev:9e843b04d885d51358a2f3de7e7a1b9264fe1915d8db83f6dac4fcf423d734a2", "ev:f57d46845581198c555f7e3d422dfab128e9779f6a66d3675e2508cda84831dd"]}
{"id": "clm:30a75cdaca9ea74fae984b3cd9319bb971853dd9609e58dc230dce1035cc84f9", "type": "statement", "text": "A March 31, 2026 OneUptime tutorial estimates that snapshot copies arrive asynchronously 15–60 minutes after the primary snapshot completes. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-03-31)", "source_url": "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-set-up-cross-region-backup-atlas/view", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:6ee6bd301c9ce3bc66271d0a429528dcba2e09dc04e34fe092598c5fb23570fd"]}
{"id": "clm:9a3efcc1c255fdd7f7019c894edee4d64c40ac0df2ad5ab9ff6bcd8b6d250d19", "type": "statement", "text": "If the primary region goes down and its snapshot is unavailable, Atlas can restore from a copied snapshot in another region. This is a backup recovery path that requires restoration; it does not itself provide automatic application failover. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/backup/cloud-backup/snapshot-distribution/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/architecture/current/disaster-recovery.md", "https://oneuptime.com/blog/post/2026-03-31-mongodb-set-up-cross-region-backup-atlas/view"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:80d840f29f4f8a282e6c0338b6e6bf6c4fbe7a83b918702ca30a26e0cccd145d", "ev:a7cf9347332532c2d5f2ab89bcab31db6188a7fceb87db0fcfc98c82e72b884f"]}
{"id": "clm:7fafa549ce5f50bb939ba6b38030bb17162b6dec3c83724411bb2ecf8ea5c233", "type": "statement", "text": "Atlas bills cross-region data transfer and additional backup-copy storage. MongoDB estimates that copying all backups to one additional region costs approximately twice the storage, with actual storage costs varying by region; selective copies and shorter copy retention can reduce unnecessary copy storage. (medium confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-20)", "source_url": "https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/billing/cluster-configuration-costs/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": ["https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/product-release-announcements/introducing-enhanced-control-for-cross-region-snapshots", "https://www.pointfive.co/efficiency-hub/inefficiencies/excessive-snapshot-retention-and-cross-region-copies-in-mongodb-atlas-cloud-backup"], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:dbd0802b4048e8e8fe932b7e0cd13dd225825052f9517c10887897b808906605", "ev:e8fcd6485889380a3f6067864c1ffc0bc71a6cb3712d2afb7d714519fbe30e72"]}
{"id": "clm:236d4b6e3e1f24ec1da7fddc2fcea85e49c1dd3eec732788caa6ae1866abc0d2", "type": "statement", "text": "A Reddit user describing an Atlas Flex cluster in me-central-1 said the live cluster and backups appeared inaccessible during a regional outage and asked whether a restore to another region could be forced. The thread verifies neither the backup configuration nor a restore outcome, so it is not evidence that configured cross-region copies failed. (low confidence) (verified as of 2026-10-23)", "source_url": "https://www.reddit.com/r/mongodb/comments/1s9g9b9/mongodb_atlas_middle_east_outage_no_access_to/", "anchor": "", "page_class": "reference", "keywords": ["Cross-Region Snapshot Copy"], "code": null, "origin": "dr", "section": "facts", "relation": "about", "score": 1.0, "also": [], "semantic_score": null, "pass": "keyword", "canonical_concept_id": "concept:5ba71bf3ab45561343f8e4444c62a1322a08c6b0ef397e98714ace77b738ac1f", "validation_status": "SUPPORTED", "evidence_ids": ["ev:e23c55d3d54b15846269ae2d0134b0cafa629466153635e43c1cb03b7a6547fb"]}
